@20001 = ~Moglus~
@20002 = ~Adventurers? Here? How did you get here?~
    @20003 = ~I used a red portal in the Evil Playroom.~
@20004 = ~A red portal? Damn, that means it stayed in place after I created it to escape. It should have disappeared on its own.~
    @20005 = ~Escape? What were you trying to escape from?~
    @20006 = ~Well, no, that didn't work. But I have to say your portal is unstable; it appears and disappears at random.~
@20007 = ~I escaped from the playroom—or rather, the torture chamber. I'm hiding here to escape Liptzitn and everything he puts me through. I was his familiar, but he delighted in inflicting the worst torments on me. You get the idea...~
@20008 = ~Damn. That means Liptzitn can find me. I escaped from the torture chamber to get away from him and everything he puts me through. I was his familiar, but he delighted in inflicting the worst torments on me. You get the idea...~
	@20009 = ~*Looking around* And you think being surrounded by all these undead is better for you?~
    @200010 = ~There are spheres in the playroom that can observe every plane. Do you really think Liptzitn can't find you with those?~
@200011 = ~These undead can't do anything to me. I'm too fast for them. And that *thing* serving as the boss moves like a manes demon.~
@200012 = ~Oh, I still have enough power to hide my presence from his spheres. If he doesn't take the portal, he won't find me. And I doubt he'll take it; he enjoys his playroom far too much...~
	@200013 = ~And what are you, exactly?~
    @200014 = ~What if he sends his minions?~
@200015 = ~I am Moglus, the divine bat.~
@200016 = ~I'd know how to hide from them. Or I'd destroy them. Believe me, I'm capable of both.~
    @200017 = ~"Divine"? Isn't that a bit of a pompous name?~
    @200018 = ~So, "Mister" Moglus, what do you propose now?~
@200019 = ~No, it isn't. Being the familiar of a lord of chaos has to be earned. You need at least a certain status for that. And being the god of bats was the minimum.~
    @200020 = ~Very well. So what do we do now that I've found you?~
@200021 = ~The bat falls silent for a few seconds, then says: Listen, I think that if you managed to get this far, you're one hell of a tough bunch. Maybe you can even rid me of Liptzitn. In that case, rather than going around in circles here, I propose to accompany you. The Material Plane surely has plenty to offer a quick mind like mine. What do you say?~
    @200022 = ~You? In my party? This has to be a joke.~
    @200023 = ~Why not? What could you offer me?~
	@200024 = ~And I suppose I should expect you to stab me in the back as soon as I turn around?~
@200025 = ~It isn't. And I wouldn't take up a place in your party. I'd follow you from a distance, simply enjoying everything your world has to offer.~
@200026 = ~I'd follow you from a distance and support you with my magical powers. Oh, and on the Material Plane, I'm invulnerable. And if something sends me back to the Abyss, I'll know how to return.~
@200027 = ~Er... no. I grant you, creatures of the Abyss are known for being evil; but not me. I have no evil inclinations, I'm simply curious. That's what Liptzitn couldn't stand about me: I didn't live up to his expectations of murder, domination, and sadism. That's why he tried to destroy me... unsuccessfully.~
	@200028 = ~All right. Welcome aboard, Moglus.~
    @200029 = ~No. I can't trust a bat from Hell. You'll stay here.~
@200030 = ~So be it.~
	@200031 = ~Well, that shouldn't be a problem for you anymore: Liptzitn is dead.~
	@200032 = ~Really? You did that? I'm impressed... Thank you, anyway.~
	@200033 = ~A demon who says "thank you"? That's unusual. Who are you, exactly?~
@200034 = ~The bat falls silent for a few seconds, then says: Listen, by killing Liptzitn, you've proved you're one hell of a tough bunch. So rather than going around in circles here, I propose to accompany you. The Material Plane surely has plenty to offer a quick mind like mine. What do you say?~
@200035 = ~Yes?~
@200036 = ~So, how are you doing, Moglus?~
@200037 = ~Very well, thank you. Your quest, this new world, these battles—it's exhilarating. Thank you again for taking me with you.~
@200038 = ~Believe me, I don't regret it.~
@200039 = ~Moglus, I'd like you to stop traveling with me.~
@200040 = ~Huh? Why? Well... I suppose it had to happen sooner or later: my greatness is overshadowing you, is that it? Anyway, your word is final, so I bid you farewell, my good master.~~Huh? Why? Well... I suppose it had to happen sooner or later: my greatness is overshadowing you, is that it? Anyway, your word is final, so I bid you farewell, my good mistress.~

@200041 = ~The Anomaly~
@200042 = ~Spatial Imprecision~
@200043 = ~Great Ghul~
@200051 = ~Joron. Killed by a cow~
@200052 = ~Gorok "The Invincible". Apparently not~
@200053 = ~Here lies Manikun. His wife is happy about it~
@200054 = ~Exterminator. He can finally rest~
@200055 = ~Deu-deu, died at 2:02~
@200056 = ~Bakum. He stinks less in death than he did in life~
@200057 = ~Piuc. Well, what's left of him...~
@200058 = ~Alan. The chicken was stronger than him~


